# `yo fix <path> --migrate explicit-copy` counts a write a loop, a closure
# called again or a function called again makes ABOVE a copy as a write after
# it, when the copy outlives one run of that region
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-24-explicit-copy-migration-misses-a-write-a-loop-makes-above-the-copy.md).
# The guard compared byte offsets only, so the four copies below (a
# parameter and a local in a `while`, a `for`, a closure called twice) were
# cloned, and the next iteration's push no longer reached them.
# `fresh_each_iteration`'s copy dies with its iteration and is still cloned.
# The trailing check proves main.yo still evaluates.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=240
